 30 April 1851", "title_original": "Stewards", "list_type": "membership", "source_id": "jewish-chronicle", "date": "1851-04-16", "citation": "Vol. VII, no. 28", "pages": "p. 223", "purpose": "A dinner in aid of the funds of the Jews' Orphan Asylum (established 5591–1831), at the London Tavern, Bishopsgate Street, on Wednesday 30 April 1851, Frederick Peel, Esq., M.P., in the chair.", "organizer_id": "jews-orphan-asylum", "place_id": "london", "beneficiary_place_id": "london", "currency": "GBP", "image": "/images/jewish-chronicle-1851-04-16-p223-portsmouth.jpg", "image_credit": "Internet Archive (from microfilm)", "iiif_manifest": "", "status": "full transcription — not yet checked", "transcriber": "Claude (draft)", "featured": "no", "notes": "Advertisement for the dinner, listing its stewards. No amounts are printed: stewards usually gave or collected toward the dinner, but this list records only their names. Tickets were one guinea each, from the stewards, the London Tavern, or J. Dias, Hon. Sec., at the office of the asylum, Tenter Ground, Goodman's Fields. 60 stewards, including the president, vice-president and treasurer. The page image is shared with the Portsmouth list on the same page."}], "roles": [{"list_id": "jews-orphan-asylum-stewards-1851", "entity_id": "", "role": "committee", "name_as_printed": "Her Royal Highness the Duchess of Kent", "address_as_printed": "", "note": "Patron"}, {"list_id": "jews-orphan-asylum-stewards-1851", "entity_id": "", "role": "committee", "name_as_printed": "His Grace the Duke of Buccleugh, K.G.", "address_as_printed": "", "note": "Patron"}, {"list_id": "jews-orphan-asylum-stewards-1851", "entity_id": "adler-nathan-marcus", "role": "committee", "name_as_printed": "The Rev. Dr. N. M. Adler", "address_as_printed": "", "note": "Patron"}, {"list_id": "jews-orphan-asylum-stewards-1851", "entity_id": "", "role": "committee", "name_as_printed": "A. L. Moses, Esq.", "address_as_printed": "", "note": "Patron"}, {"list_id": "jews-orpha